{title: When Morning Gilds the Skies}
{artist: German hymn, tr. Edward Caswall / Joseph Barnby}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Anthem}
{flow: Opening}
{key: C}
{tempo: 115}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Trinity Hymnal (Philadelphia, Pennsylvania: Orthodox Presbyterian Church, 1961), # 131)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]When [Dm]morning [F]gilds [Dm]the [G7]skies__[F]__
[F]My [Am]heart awaking [D7]cries:__[Em]__
[D7]May [G]Je[C]sus [D7]Christ be [G]praised!
[G]A[C]like at work and [G7]prayer,__[Em]__
[Em]To [C]Jesus [Bm]I [D7]re[G]pair:__[Em]__
[Em]May [C7]Jesus [F]Christ [Dm]be__[G7]__ [C]praised!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Does [Dm]sadness [F]fill [Dm]my [G7]mind?__[F]__
[F]A [Am]solace here I [D7]find,__[Em]__
[D7]May [G]J[C]esus [D7]Christ be [G]praised!
[G]Or [C]fades my earthly [G7]bliss?__[Em]__
[Em]My [C]comfort [Bm]still [D7]is [G]this,__[Em]__
[Em]May [C7]Jesus [F]Christ [Dm]be__[G7]__ [C]praised!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]In [Dm]Heav’n’s e[F]ter[Dm]nal [G7]bliss__[F]__
[F]The [Am]loveliest strain is [D7]this,__[Em]__
[D7]May [G]Je[C]sus [D7]Christ be [G]praised!
[G]Let [C]earth, and sea and [G7]sky__[Em]__
[Em]From [C]depth to [Bm]height [D7]re[G]ply,__[Em]__
[Em]May [C7]Jesus [F]Christ [Dm]be__[G7]__ [C]praised!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]Be [Dm]this, while [F]life [Dm]is [G7]mine,__[F]__
[F]My [Am]canticle di[D7]vine:__[Em]__
[D7]May [G]Je[C]sus [D7]Christ be [G]praised!
[G]Sing [C]this eternal [G7]song__[Em]__
[Em]Through [C]all the [Bm]ag[D7]es [G]long:__[Em]__
[Em]May [C7]Jesus [F]Christ [Dm]be__[G7]__ [C]praised!
{end_of_verse}
